## Scope of this licence

The MIT licence above covers **the code and documentation in this repository
only** — everything under `scripts/`, `demo/`, `agents/`, `docs/`, `scoring/`, and
the Markdown at the repository root.

**It does not cover the contents of `data/raw/`.** Those files are third-party
data redistributed under their own terms:

- **O\*NET 30.3 Database** (`data/raw/onet_*.txt`, `onet_*.html`) — by the U.S.
  Department of Labor, Employment and Training Administration (USDOL/ETA), used
  under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)**
  licence. The licence text as retrieved is committed at
  `data/raw/onet_license_db.txt`. Attribution is mandatory and verbatim; the
  required block and the rules for reproducing it are in
  `docs/onet-attribution.md`.

  > This product includes information from the O\*NET 30.3 Database by the U.S.
  > Department of Labor, Employment and Training Administration (USDOL/ETA).
  > Used under the CC BY 4.0 license. O\*NET® is a trademark of USDOL/ETA.
  >
  > TitleTrack has modified all or some of this information. USDOL/ETA has not
  > approved, endorsed, or tested these modifications.

- **NYC Open Data** (`data/raw/k397_*`, `data/raw/4ptz*`) — snapshots of the NYC
  Citywide Payroll Data (`k397-673e`) and the DCAS Annual Examination Schedule
  (`4ptz-hmtc`), published by the City of New York under the NYC Open Data terms
  of use. Retrieval dates and dataset vintages are recorded in
  `docs/data-sources-and-hazards.md`.

Reusing anything from `data/raw/` means complying with the upstream terms, not
this MIT grant.
